    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than three years from the date of this decision.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended by Section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications: [PL-00-001, PL-02-120, Fire Strategy, EX-02-120, EX-02-121, EX-02-122, EX-02-123, EX-03-120, EX-03-121, Design and Access Statement, PL-02-120, PR-02-121, PL-02-123, PL-03-120 received 13/05/2026\r\nPR-02-122 Rev A, PL-03-121 Rev B received 08/07/2026].\r\nReason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building, unless otherwise shown on the approved plans.\r\nReason: In order to safeguard the appearance of the area.",
    "Condition : 4 - The windows formed in the north elevation shall be obscure-glazed and non-opening below 1.7 metres above internal floor level. The windows shall not be repaired or replaced otherwise than in accordance with the requirements of this condition. \r\nReason: In order to protect neighbours' privacy\r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - The window(s) to be fitted on the [front/rear] roof face of the dwelling shall be black-framed and traditional, conservation-style.\r\nReason: In order to safeguard the architectural and historic interest of the [conservation area/listed building]."
